+# CISA "When to Issue VEX Information" — issuance is a business decision, the under_investigation → final-status lifecycle, timestamp-only reaffirmation, and the upstream-status inheritance caution: the VEX publishing layer that the CSAF VEX profile does not carry
+
+source: S057 — https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/when-issue-vex-information — capture corpus/source-snapshots/round-39/S057.txt (275 lines, 17,971 bytes; sha256 11c8d6d684448a1ae049ecf4881cd98172fad7333a9fd7829e6b12c9b5d64f2f): title L2, publication date L3, purpose L11-L15, business-decision sentence L12-L14, "not determined by a strict protocol" L79-L81, event triggers L84/L104/L114/L142/L153, status lifecycle L132-L135, timestamp reaffirmation L136-L138, exploitation degree plus action_statement L117-L122, KEV pointer L127-L130, CVD independence L143-L144, legal obligations L154-L157, inheritance caution L183-L186, inheritance allowance L187-L191, multiple supply chain paths L192-L199, trust L201-L212, open-source section L215-L227
+verified-at: 2026-10-26 (capture re-fetched and re-normalized this day: PDF https://www.cisa.gov/sites/default/files/2023-11/When-to-Issue-a-VEX-508c.pdf, HTTP 200, 235,270 bytes, sha256 cbcbd77af32c589eaf85aef4e3911b133fd95ccdedd80b56b40e9c0909450d99 at 2026-10-26T19:31:07Z; my `pdftotext` + whitespace-collapse run reproduced the landed capture byte for byte — `cmp` clean, 275 lines, 17,971 bytes, sha256 11c8d6d6…)
